HUMAN: HUD polish pass vs user reference — 7 concrete deltas from side-by-side comparison.
FIND F19 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html#"nhudBuildCenter" what="center bracket arcs built but visually absent in flight; ref shows two large cyan curved brackets flanking the reticle" fix="arcs ~46vh tall, ~30vw apart, 2px solid var(--nh-cyan) at 55% opacity, border-radius-based curve (border-left arc technique) or inline SVG paths; ensure z-order above canvas below panels; verify visible in a flight screenshot" ref=- dep=-
FIND F20 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html#"updateCenterHUD" what="speed/alt value chips render but the vertical tick tape columns do not" fix="each tape: 5 tick labels (speed: rounded 100s descending; alt: rounded 100ft) in a masked 220px column, minor tick marks between, translateY sliding with value; chips stay centered; dirty-check to 1-unit steps" ref=- dep=F19
FIND F21 sev=M tag=quality at=flight-sim3.html#"#instruments" what="left cluster stacks SPD/ALT/HDG vertically; ref is a single horizontal 3-column card with labels above values" fix="restyle to one nhud-panel row of three cells (label small-caps above, mono value+unit below), width ~380px; keep ids speed/altitude/heading and their writers untouched" ref=- dep=-
